   "issue": "\"A locally realizing family inherits the global constraints of the system: all its local discriminants are images of the one global class `d`, its finite Hasse invariants are trivial at almost every place, and the product ... is one\" \u2014 all three require admissibility. `IsLocalRealization` constrains the real forms only through `sigPos_real`, so for a non-admissible `I` the real discriminant need not be the image of `d` and `finiteHasse` may have infinite support. The same unconditional claim is repeated in the Main results bullet at lines 58-62.",
